# FontAwesome icons first

Use FontAwesome from `@expo/vector-icons` for UI glyphs. Hand-drawn SVG is a fallback, not the default.

## Order

1. Use an existing named export from `components/chrome/icons.tsx` if one already matches.
2. Otherwise use a FontAwesome glyph (`bars`, `cog`, `key`, `comment`, `image`, `eye`, …). Add a named wrapper in `icons.tsx` when the same glyph is reused or needs a default size/color.
3. If no FontAwesome glyph is a reasonable match, then add a custom SVG in `icons.tsx`.

Browse names at https://icons.expo.fyi (FontAwesome set). Import with `import FontAwesome from "@expo/vector-icons/FontAwesome"`.

## Defaults

- Menu items: 14px, `colors.pen`
- Toolbar / field buttons: 16px
- Muted field controls (e.g. show password): `colors.ink400`
- Preload `FontAwesome.font` in `app/_layout.tsx` via `useFonts` so icons do not flash empty

## Do not replace with FontAwesome

- Brand logos (Google, Facebook) — keep the official colored SVGs
- Charts or decorative illustrations (e.g. score ring)

Icon *meaning* still follows the web app. The glyph source may be FontAwesome instead of copied Heroicons paths.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — copy a Heroicons path when FontAwesome already has it
<Svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><Path d="M3.75 6.75h16.5…" /></Svg>

// ✅ GOOD
<FontAwesome name="bars" size={16} color={colors.pen} />
```
